    description:
      "A systematic review of 40 papers found cohort studies link volunteering to lower depression and higher wellbeing, and a meta-analysis of five cohorts found volunteers had about 22 percent lower mortality risk; the few randomized trials did not confirm the mental-health effects. A meta-analysis of older adults found volunteering reduced adjusted mortality risk by about a quarter. In the Health and Retirement Study, volunteers used more preventive care and spent fewer nights in hospital, and starting to volunteer later in life was followed by slower progression of disability, especially at higher intensity. Effects are observational and probably partly selection, but the direction is consistent.",
